acy\nTheses and Capstones\nGraduation\nCertify Online\nContinuing to a Doctoral Program\nDoctoral Degree Policies and Procedures\nCredit Hour Requirements\nResidency Requirement\nCandidacy, Quals\nGraduate Faculty\nDissertation\nGraduation\nGraduate Certificate Verification\nGraduation Ceremony\nInstitutional Rules, Policies and Procedures\nAcademic Dishonesty\nStudent Code of Conduct\nResponsible Conduct of Research\nRestricted Research\nGrievance Procedures\nAbout Us\nGraduate College Staff\nGive\nThe\nGraduate\nCollege\nApply\nStudent Resources\nGraduation\nUC to a Higher Degree\nGraduate students play a critical role in the University of Cincinnati's status as a comprehensive research-intensive university. Through the Graduate College's 400+ graduate degree and certificate programs, University of Cincinnati graduate students generate knowledge and discovery that benefit society.\nAt the University of Cincinnati Graduate College, we invest in tomorrow\u2019s leaders and professionals.\nWhat are you interested in?\nThe University of Cincinnati offers nearly 400 graduate programs, from master\u2019s and doctoral degree programs to graduate certificates and artist diplomas. Find your passion:\nKeywords\nSearch for programs\nProgram Award\nInterest\nLocation\n{{degree.name}}\n{{interestArea.name}}\n{{location.name}}\nClear All Filters\nremove\nremove\nremove\nremove\nLoading\nNo programs to show. Try Broadening Your Search\n{{(programs | collegeFilter:colleges | degreesFilter:degrees | interestAreasFilter:interestAreas | locationsFilter:locations | searchString:keyword).length}} Programs Found\nCLOSE\n{{program.baseInfo.planDescription}}\n{{(program.baseInfo.subPlanDescription != 'NONE' ? program.baseInfo.subPlanDescription : '')}}\n{{program.baseInfo.planDescription}}\n{{program.baseInfo.degree == \"MIN\" ? \"Declare\" : \"Apply\"}}\nRequest Information\nProgram Award:\n{{program.baseInfo.degreeBucket}} ({{program.baseInfo.degree}})\nCollege:\n{{program.baseInfo.organizationDescription}}\nLocation:\n{{program.baseInfo.location}}\nFull-time program duration:\n{{program.baseInfo.duration}} {{program.baseInfo.durationUnit}}\n{{program.baseInfo.subPlanDescription}}\nLearn More\nCompare\nremove\nCompare All\nRemove All\nClose\n{{cmpProgram.baseInfo.planDescription}}\n{{cmpProgram.baseInfo.degree}}\nFull-time program Duration\n{{cmpProgram.baseInfo.duration}} {{cmpProgram.baseInfo.durationUnit}}\nWhat you'll learn\nLocation\n{{cmpProgram.baseInfo.location}}\n{{cmpProgram.baseInfo.degree == \"MIN\" ? \"Declare\" : \"Apply\"}}\nLearn More\nProfessional Development\nPrepare for your future career at UC. Graduate College events and programs prepare graduate students to be tomorrow\u2019s leaders and professionals.\nA City for Young Professionals\nCincinnati provides the perfect backdrop for the graduate experience, offering academic-corporate partnerships, exciting career opportunities and all the big-city amenities in an area with an affordable cost of living.\nInnovation and Discovery\nWith a long history of breakthroughs across various fields and a reputation as a \u201cresearch heavyweight,\u201d UC is a thriving hub for future-leaning advancement. #NextLivesHere\nI know that I will leave UC with lifelong networks, particularly with my professors who have been instrumental in my current and future success at UC.\nMaurice Adkins\nPhD, History\n#5\nMost welcoming for international students (ISB)\n$45M\nIn graduate tuition scholarships\n#35\nTop public school in research & development (NSF)\nGraduate College News\n1\nStill the top \u2018cat\nOctober 20, 2026\nThe University of Cincinnati Bearcat mascot was voted Cincinnati\u2019s favorite mascot in a Cincinnati Enquirer reader poll, earning 45.1% of the vote and topping other local favorites.\n2\nGot three minutes? Present your research for a chance to win $1,500\nOctober 19, 2026\nThe University of Cincinnati\u2019s Three Minute Thesis (3MT) Competition challenges graduate students to explain their research or scholarship to people outside their field in just three minutes using a single slide. Applications for the 2027 competition open Sunday, Nov. 1, 2026, giving graduate students a chance to sharpen a skill that can make a difference far beyond graduate school.\n3\nEnvironmental engineer researching methods to monitor river quality\nOctober 16, 2026\nPradeep Ramtel has been conducting research on river water since he was an undergraduate student in Nepal. He is currently a PhD student at the University of Cincinnati and is studying under Associate Professor Dongmei Feng. His research uses collected data and machine learning to better assess risks to river water quality and prepare for problems before they arise. Recently, he was named Graduate Student Engineer of the Month by UC's College of Engineering and Applied Science.\nExplore More News\nUpcoming Dissertation Defenses\nTyler Pritschau, CEAS\nWed, 28 Oct 2026\nAerospace Engineering, Doctor of Philosophy\nMitansh Tripathi, CEAS\nWed, 28 Oct 2026\nAerospace Engineering, Doctor of Philosophy\nSeyed Aref Golsorkhi, CEAS\nThu, 29 Oct 2026\nMaterials Science, Doctor of Philosophy\n310 Van Wormer Hall\nP.O. Box 210627\nCincinnati, OH 45221\n513-556-4335\ngrad.info@uc.edu\nUC Tools\nCanopy & Canvas\nEnrollment Services\nEmail\nCatalyst\nBearcat Portal\nShuttle Tracker\nIT Help\nUC VPN\nBearcats Landing\nAbout Us\nMaps & Directions\nJobs\nNews\nCommunity Impact\nGovernance & Policies\nDirectory\nEvents Calendar\nUniversity of Cincinnati | 2600 Clifton Ave. | Cincinnati, OH 45221 | ph: (513) 556-6000\nAlerts | Clery and HEOA Notice | Notice of Non-Discrimination | Statement of Commitment | Syllabi Archive | eAccessibility Concern | Privacy Statement | Free Speech | Copyright Information | Accreditation\n\u00a9 2026 University of Cincinnati\n310 Van Wormer Hall\nP.O. Box 210627\nCincinnati, OH 45221\n513-556-4335\n\u00a9 2026 University of Cincinnati", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://ww